.TH AT 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
at \- planifie un travail unique / queue jobs for later execution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B at
[-f file] [-m] time [date] [+ N units]
.br
.B batch

.br
.B atq

.br
.B atrm
job...
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads commands from the standard input (or -f file) and runs them once at the given time through atd. Time: HH:MM, HHMM, now, noon, midnight, teatime, with
am/pm; date: today, tomorrow, Month DD [YYYY], DD.MM.YYYY, MM/DD/YYYY; increments: + N minutes|hours|days|weeks. batch runs the job when the load average drops
below 1.5. atq lists the pending jobs and atrm removes them. Jobs are stored in /var/spool/cron/atjobs.
.SH SEE ALSO
crontab(1), crond(1)
